<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Universal Links — DISABLED until this app is on a PAID Apple Developer
	  Program team. Free "Personal Team" accounts cannot provision the
	  Associated Domains capability, so enabling it breaks signing.
	  (MitraTrip.entitlements carries the same note for the same reason.)

	  WHY THIS APP: shared expenses arrive over `quaramoney://split`, a custom
	  URL scheme. Custom schemes carry no origin attestation — any app, web page
	  or QR code can invoke one, and nothing guarantees THIS app is the one that
	  receives a link another app sends. Universal Links are the authenticated
	  alternative, and the entitlement belongs on the RECEIVING app: MitraTrip
	  only opens an https URL, which needs no capability at all.

	  Until then the mitigation is procedural and holds: ImportSharedExpenseView
	  never auto-imports, every amount is shown before it is written, and the
	  sender's claimed identity (`SharedExpenseSource.app`) is treated as an
	  unverified claim rather than a trust badge.

	  To turn Universal Links on once enrolled in the paid program:
	    1. In the Apple Developer portal, enable "Associated Domains" on the
	       App ID (uk.dormmy.QuaraMoney).
	    2. Uncomment the entitlement below and rebuild (automatic signing will
	       refresh the provisioning profile).
	    3. Add this app to the apple-app-site-association file already planned
	       for mitratrip.app — one AASA can claim several apps on different
	       paths, so no second domain is needed:

	         { "applinks": { "details": [
	             { "appIDs": ["852VUPUNPH.mitratrip.app"],
	               "components": [{ "/": "/trip/*" }, { "/": "/invite/*" }] },
	             { "appIDs": ["852VUPUNPH.uk.dormmy.QuaraMoney"],
	               "components": [{ "/": "/import/*" }] }
	         ]}}

	    4. Teach SplitExpenseService.canHandle to accept
	       https://mitratrip.app/import/... alongside the existing scheme, and
	       keep the scheme working for links already in the wild.

	  <key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	  <array>
	      <string>applinks:mitratrip.app</string>
	  </array>
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
